# Line endings. Every file in the working tree is LF, whatever wrote it last.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` here, so without this rule a `git checkout` or
# `git restore` rewrites a file stored with line feed endings into
# carriage-return line-feed endings, while every editor and shell tool used
# here writes line feeds. A file's endings then depend on what touched it
# last, which breaks anything that reads a file byte for byte.

* text=auto eol=lf
